.TH CLANKY 1
.SH NAME
clanky \- GPU-rendered terminal for coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clanky
.RB [ --headless ]
.RB [ --socket " PATH" ]
.RB [ --config " PATH" ]
.br
.B clanky
.RB [ --help | -h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Clanky is a Linux terminal with tabs, split panes, and a local agent socket.
Agent access to a graphical terminal is disabled by default.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --headless
Run without a graphical window.
.TP
.BI --socket " PATH"
Use PATH for the agent socket. Its parent directory must be private and owned
by the current user. An existing socket is not removed.
.TP
.BI --config " PATH"
Read configuration from PATH.
.TP
.BR --help , " -h"
Print usage and keyboard shortcuts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/clanky/config.json
Default configuration when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is set.
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/clanky/config.json
Default configuration otherwise. A missing default file uses built-in defaults.
.SH KEYBOARD
Ctrl+Shift+T opens a tab; Ctrl+Shift+D and Ctrl+Shift+E split a pane.
Ctrl+Shift+W closes a pane; Ctrl+Tab switches tabs. Ctrl+Shift+A toggles
agent access to the focused pane. Ctrl+Shift+P opens the palette and
Ctrl+Shift+B toggles the sidebar. Ctrl+= and Ctrl+- zoom; Ctrl+0 resets zoom.
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://github.com/rustytensor/clanky
Clanky project
.UE
